<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Boland Bank yr headline shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Boland Bank yr headline shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		 (millions of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts) 275.0   vs  210.9</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	    276.0   vs  210.9</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)     55.0   making 94.0 vs 77.7</p>
<p>    Total income	 416.85  vs  335.73</p>
<p>    Interest earned  1,237.31  vs  901.59</p>
<p>Net interest</p>
<p>    income		 303.52  vs  251.22</p>
<p>Other operating</p>
<p>    income		 209.37  vs  144.60</p>
<p>    Risk provisions     96.04  vs   60.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		112.89  vs   90.50</p>
<p>    Tax			6.09  vs   19.81</p>
<p>    Interest paid	933.79  vs  650.36</p>
<p>Div payable July 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Boland Bank Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE: The results for the bank are the last before it is delisted and merges with NBS Holdings Ltd and directors said they were unable to make an independent forecast of the merged group's performance. But they were positive that it could make a significant contribution to inreased group profits in the new financial year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
